Comment: Coverage floors for tools/coverage/measure.R, per OS because each
 builds a different TLS backend. Raise a floor when coverage rises; never
 lower one to make CI pass. A drop means code lost its tests, or code
 arrived without them. Until 2026-11-04 measure.R matched the pre-W2 zu_
 prefix, so the own_c floors were set on init.c alone; the whole C core,
 measured with the HTTP/2 and gRPC servers running, clears them as set.
 fuzz_reach is tools/coverage/fuzz-lcov.sh over the committed corpus: how
 much of the C core some fuzz target runs on hostile input, kept apart from
 the floors above because a fuzzed line is not a checked one (#230).
fuzz_reach: 64
own_c_macos: 91.5
r_macos: 90
own_c_linux: 89
r_linux: 90
